# webkitgtk-bundle/versions.env
# Single source of truth for pinned dependency versions. Update this file (and only
# this file) when bumping a version; build-in-container.sh sources it verbatim.

WEBKITGTK_VERSION=2.52.5
GLIB_VERSION=2.84.4
CAIRO_VERSION=1.18.4
PANGO_VERSION=1.56.4
GDK_PIXBUF_VERSION=2.42.12
GTK4_VERSION=4.18.6
LIBSOUP_VERSION=3.6.5
ICU_VERSION=77-1
LIBTASN1_VERSION=4.20.0
SQLITE_YEAR=2026
SQLITE_VERSION=3530400
LCMS2_VERSION=2.17
LIBWEBP_VERSION=1.6.0
OPENJPEG_VERSION=2.5.3
LIBGUDEV_VERSION=238
LIBSECRET_VERSION=0.21.7
MESA_VERSION=25.1.8
GSTREAMER_VERSION=1.26.5
WPEBACKEND_FDO_VERSION=1.14.2
# libwpe: NOT in the original plan's versions.env -- discovered as a real, previously
# unaccounted-for dependency while implementing Task 5. wpebackend-fdo's own
# meson.build does `dependency('wpe-1.0', ..., fallback: ['libwpe', 'libwpe_dep'])`,
# i.e. it hard-requires libwpe (WPE's core windowing-abstraction library) and will
# only silently build it as a meson subproject if a matching system copy isn't
# findable via pkg-config -- neither of which this from-source, explicit-versioning
# build wants to rely on implicitly. Built explicitly, from source, the same way as
# every other dependency in this chain.
LIBWPE_VERSION=1.16.3
HARFBUZZ_VERSION=14.3.0
GRAPHENE_VERSION=1.10.8
LIBPSL_VERSION=0.21.5
# TLS backend chain for libsoup/GIO -- glib-networking is the GIO TLS backend module
# libsoup delegates to at runtime; it needs a real TLS implementation, which for the
# GNOME stack (and glib-networking's own default, non-second-guessed choice per its
# meson.options) is GnuTLS, not OpenSSL. GMP/Nettle/p11-kit are GnuTLS's own from-source
# dependency chain (bignum arithmetic, the crypto primitives library, and PKCS#11/system
# trust-store integration respectively).
GMP_VERSION=6.3.0
NETTLE_VERSION=3.10.2
P11KIT_VERSION=0.26.5
GNUTLS_VERSION=3.8.13
GLIB_NETWORKING_VERSION=2.80.1
# Task 8 post-review correction (2026-08-10): vendored from source instead of relying
# on the build container's system packages -- `ldd` run against the packaged tarball
# OUTSIDE the build container (this plan's first time actually testing that way)
# found libjpeg.so.62 (a Debian-*specific* soname, unsatisfiable as-is on most other
# distros), libxml2, and libxslt all missing on a real target machine. All three are
# genuinely needed for real web-content rendering (WebKitGTK's own OptionsGTK.cmake
# has unconditional `find_package(JPEG REQUIRED)` / `find_package(LibXml2 ...
# REQUIRED)` calls), so -- unlike gamepad/spellcheck/hyphenation, which were simply
# disabled -- these are now built from source into $PREFIX the same way as every
# other real dependency in this chain, sidestepping the soname/portability problem
# entirely. See build-in-container.sh's libjpeg-turbo/libxml2/libxslt section and
# Containerfile's matching correction comment for the full reasoning.
# LIBXML2_VERSION: originally pinned to 2.14.6 (the newest release in what looked
# like the established "2.14" stable series at the time) -- a REAL bug, not just a
# style choice: libxslt 1.1.45's own ./configure hard-requires
# "libxml >= 2.15.1" ("Version 2.14.6 found. You need at least libxml2 2.15.1 for
# this version of libxslt" -- caught by an actual full rebuild failing at exactly
# this check, not discovered by reading release notes in advance). Bumped to 2.15.3
# (the newest point release in the 2.15 series at the time of this fix) to satisfy
# libxslt's real minimum.
LIBJPEG_TURBO_VERSION=3.2.0
LIBXML2_VERSION=2.15.3
LIBXSLT_VERSION=1.1.45
# 2026-08-18 crash fix (bug report plan/bug-reports/report1-stable.md): freetype was
# previously left to the HOST (see build-in-container.sh's own comment on the
# deliberately-unvendored set) -- a real ABI trap, not just a portability nicety.
# FreeType 2.13.0 added an `FT_Bool read_variable` field to FT_ColorStopIterator,
# which is embedded BY VALUE in FT_ColorLine -> FT_Paint*Gradient -> the
# FT_COLR_Paint union. Built against Debian 12's 2.12.1 headers, FT_COLR_Paint is
# 80 bytes; on any host with >= 2.13.0 (Fedora 38+, Ubuntu 24.04+, Arch) the runtime
# FT_Get_Paint writes 88 bytes at shifted offsets into Skia's stack-allocated copy.
# colrv1_configure_skpaint then reads current_color_stop out of the wrong offset and
# indexes a 2-element std::vector with 16384 -> __glibcxx_assert -> SIGABRT of the
# whole WebKitWebProcess, reproducibly, on any COLRv1 color font (Fedora ships Noto
# Color Emoji as COLRv1; Arch ships it as CBDT bitmap, which is why this never
# reproduced on the dev machine). Vendoring is the only real fix: bumping the
# container base just inverts the mismatch for older hosts, and bounds-checking Skia
# would leave the 8-byte stack overwrite in place.
FREETYPE_VERSION=2.14.3
